WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.000
How long does a payment take to clear? Time is continuous: two

00:04.100 --> 00:08.762
minutes, two point five, two point five one... So what's the probability

00:08.862 --> 00:13.457
that it takes exactly three minutes, to infinitely many decimal places?

00:15.550 --> 00:18.163
The answer is zero, and understanding why leads

00:18.263 --> 00:20.125
straight to the idea of a density.

00:21.216 --> 00:25.688
Record thousands of payments and draw a histogram, with bars two minutes

00:25.788 --> 00:29.625
wide. Make each bar's area, not its height, equal to the share

00:29.725 --> 00:33.054
of payments in that range. Then the total area is one.

00:33.150 --> 00:37.271
Now make the bars narrower. One minute. Half a minute. A tenth

00:37.371 --> 00:41.492
of a minute. The outline stops being jagged and settles onto a

00:41.592 --> 00:46.189
smooth curve. That curve is the probability density function, f of y.

00:47.983 --> 00:51.165
Probabilities are now areas under the curve. The chance

00:51.265 --> 00:53.971
a payment takes between two and four minutes is

00:54.071 --> 00:57.313
the area between two and four: about thirty-six percent.

00:57.400 --> 01:02.910
And the probability of exactly three minutes? Shrink an interval around three.

01:03.010 --> 01:06.867
The area shrinks with it, all the way to zero. A single

01:06.967 --> 01:11.471
point has no width, so it has no area. For continuous variables,

01:11.571 --> 01:16.291
individual values have probability zero, and only intervals matter.

01:17.883 --> 01:23.536
Finally, the distribution function, capital F of y: the probability of being

01:23.636 --> 01:27.018
at most y, which is the area to the left of y.

01:27.118 --> 01:31.105
Sweep y across, and watch that area accumulate into F.

01:31.200 --> 01:35.517
F climbs fastest where the density is tallest, and it flattens out at

01:35.617 --> 01:39.167
one. In fact the density is exactly the slope of F. For a

01:39.267 --> 01:43.713
discrete variable, F would be a staircase that jumps at each value; for

01:43.813 --> 01:47.426
a continuous one, it rises smoothly, with no jumps at all.

01:48.516 --> 01:51.748
So: a density is what a histogram becomes when the

01:51.848 --> 01:56.146
bars are infinitely thin. Probabilities are areas under it. Single

01:56.246 --> 02:00.477
points get probability zero. And the distribution function is the

02:00.577 --> 02:04.142
area accumulated so far, with the density as its slope.
